---
Foo: Bar
# Frontmatter Comment
---

This fixture pins the automatic `headings` export (§20) in the **nested** shape the
retired `plugin-extract-heading` used to inject. `renderer-solid` now builds that
outline from the AST, so `sandbox/heading` renders byte-identically without the
plugin. The `[[task.heading.extract]]` block is the plugin's replacement: the same
headings as a **flat** array with `depth`. A plain heading has no head, so its row
carries only `depth` and `inner_text`; `Foo Bar` shows what a head adds (`title`).

A heading is a heading wherever the lexer finds one — inside a section, inside an
HTML comment, or inside a `{{{…}}}` block that no `bind` stage consumed. A code
fence is not:

# Lorem Isum

###[foo-bar]("Foo Bar") Foo Bar

## Bar Foo


<!--
# Markdown Comment
-->

# Hiz


{{{toml[dataY]
# Bind Comment
}}}

```
## Codefence Comment
```

